# Task 19 - make the unit-script assertion non-tautological

Wave: 5 lane B
Worktree: /home/mei/nixos-wt/thinkpad-zero-touch-install-wave5 (branch thinkpad-zero-touch-install/wave5)
Base: main 7689b0c (HEAD parent at commit time: 006c314, a sibling-lane commit on the same branch)
Commit: be2ac143bf07f288bcf50c490bfe48149e935e8f `test(iso): make the unit-script assertion non-tautological`
Plan: .omo/plans/thinkpad-zero-touch-install.md todo 19 (closes F2 "near-tautological assertion" nit)

## What changed

tests/dendritic-config-eval.nix, ISO installer wall (was line 292):

    -assert hasInfix "install" isoAutoinstallUnit.script;
    +# Invocation, not tautology: a bare `hasInfix "install"` matched the
    +# wrapper's own `/nix/store/...-install/bin/install` store path.
    +assert hasInfix (builtins.unsafeDiscardStringContext flake.apps.x86_64-linux.install.program) isoAutoinstallUnit.script;
    +assert hasInfix "--host antagony" isoAutoinstallUnit.script;
     assert hasInfix "--rescue-identity" isoAutoinstallUnit.script;

No other assertion weakened, renumbered, or removed; `git show --stat HEAD` = this one file only
(1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)).

## Why

The unit script is:

    /nix/store/<hash>-install/bin/install --host antagony --yes --rescue-identity

`hasInfix "install" ... .script` matched the wrapper's OWN store path (`...-install/bin/install`),
so it could only fail if the whole program reference disappeared - it never proved the invocation
or the flags. The replacement pins (a) the wrapper store path derived from the flake app, and
(b) the `--host antagony` plan flag; the existing `--rescue-identity` assertion is retained.
`unsafeDiscardStringContext` is required: the app program is a store-path string, and Nix rejects
a store-path string used as a regex pattern (`.error: the string ... is not allowed to refer to a
store path`). The script string keeps its context and read-only use is unaffected.

