Scratch tree: /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch (tar copy of the worktree, .git excluded).

Flip A - drop ` --host ${host}` from the unit script (old tautology would still pass):

    $ sed -i 's/ --host [^ ]*//' /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/modules/flake/iso-images.nix
    # line 107 -> "${config.flake.apps.x86_64-linux.install.program} --yes --rescue-identity"
    $ nix-instantiate --eval --strict --expr 'import /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/tests/dendritic-config-eval.nix {}'
    error: assertion '(hasInfix "--host antagony" (isoAutoinstallUnit).script)' failed
           at /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/tests/dendritic-config-eval.nix:295:1
    RC=1

Flip B - strip the leading wrapper store-path token from the unit script:

    $ sed -i '/--rescue-identity/ s|^\( *\)[^ ]* |\1|' /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/modules/flake/iso-images.nix
    # line 107 -> "            --host ${host} --yes --rescue-identity"
    $ nix-instantiate --eval --strict --expr 'import /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/tests/dendritic-config-eval.nix {}'
    error: assertion '(hasInfix ((builtins).unsafeDiscardStringContext (flake).apps.x86_64-linux.install.program) (isoAutoinstallUnit).script)' failed
           at /tmp/ulw-t19-scratch/tests/dendritic-config-eval.nix:294:1
    RC=1

Both flips fail at exactly the tightened assertions; flip A fails on a mutation the old
`hasInfix "install"` assertion would have accepted, which is the point of the tightening.

